#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:2
msgid "Writing software for Silkie"
msgstr "为 Silkie 开发软件"

#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:4
msgid ""
"Silkie is a fork of the **kitty terminal emulator**. kitty extends the traditional VT/xterm-style"
" terminal protocol with its own graphics, keyboard, and other protocols. **Kittens** are kitty's "
"companion tools and plugins; they use terminal capabilities and can add functionality to kitty. "
"Silkie adds further terminal protocols and the :doc:`show_pointer tool <show-pointer>`."
msgstr ""
"Silkie 是 **kitty 终端模拟器** 的一个分支。kitty 在传统的 VT/xterm 风格终端协议上扩展了图形、键盘及其他协议。**Kittens** 是 kitty "
"的配套工具和插件，使用终端能力并可为 kitty 增添功能。Silkie 增加了更多终端协议和 :doc:`show_pointer 工具 <show-pointer>`。"

#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:10
msgid ""
"Silkie's behavior is documented in several places: terminal standards, kitty's manuals, and "
"Silkie's extension specifications. This guide links to each source and the relevant "
"implementation files."
msgstr "Silkie 的行为分散记录在终端标准、kitty 手册和 Silkie 扩展规范中。本指南提供这些资料及相关实现文件的链接。"

#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:15
msgid "Source and version"
msgstr "源代码与版本"

#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:17
msgid "Silkie's source is on the `silkie branch <https://github.com/adamdeprince/silkie/tree/silkie>`_."
msgstr "Silkie 源代码位于 `silkie 分支 <https://github.com/adamdeprince/silkie/tree/silkie>`_。"

#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:20
msgid ""
"Upstream kitty manuals may describe behavior that differs from your Silkie build. The source for "
"your version shows how a feature is implemented. Runtime capability queries tell your application"
" which extensions, versions, and optional features are available."
msgstr "上游 kitty 手册描述的行为可能与所用 Silkie 构建不同。对应版本的源代码展示了功能的实现方式。运行时能力查询则告诉应用哪些扩展、版本和可选功能可用。"

#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:26
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "入门"

#. Translated reference labels preserve the original explicit section targets.
#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:28
msgid ""
"If you are new to kitty, the `kitty overview <https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/>`_ introduces the "
"terminal, and the `kitten overview <https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/kittens_intro/>`_ introduces "
"its tools and plugins. The `terminal foundations`_ and `inherited kitty protocols`_ below cover "
"the standards and protocols that Silkie builds on."
msgstr ""
"如果尚不熟悉 kitty，`kitty 概览 <https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/>`_ 介绍终端本身，`kitten 概览 "
"<https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/kittens_intro/>`_ 介绍配套工具与插件。下文的 `终端基础 <terminal foundations_>`_ "
"和 `继承的 kitty 协议 <inherited kitty protocols_>`_ 介绍 Silkie 所依赖的标准与协议。 #noqa"

#. Translated reference labels preserve the original explicit section targets.
#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:34
msgid ""
"To add a Silkie feature to your application, start with :doc:`capabilities-protocol` and :doc"
":`extension-framing`, then choose the protocols you need from the `Silkie extension map`_. Each "
"specification explains how to discover support, use the feature, and clean up afterward, "
"including any platform limits. Test your application in the target terminal and provide a "
"fallback when a feature is unavailable."
msgstr ""
"要为应用添加 Silkie 功能，请先阅读 :doc:`capabilities-protocol` 和 :doc:`extension-framing`，再从 `Silkie 扩展导览 "
"<Silkie extension map_>`_ 选择所需协议。每项规范都说明如何探测支持、使用功能及完成清理，并列出平台限制。请在目标终端中测试应用，并为不可用功能提供回退方案。 #noqa"

#. Translated reference labels preserve the original explicit section targets.
#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:41
msgid ""
"For kittens, terminal user interfaces, remote-control clients, and shell integration, see `kitten"
" and application APIs`_. The `implementation map`_ points to the relevant code if you want to "
"investigate behavior or contribute a change to Silkie."
msgstr ""
"开发 kitten、终端用户界面、远程控制客户端和 shell 集成时，参阅 `Kitten 与应用 API <kitten and application APIs_>`_。若要调查行为或为 "
"Silkie 贡献修改，`实现导览 <implementation map_>`_ 可引导你找到相关代码。 #noqa"

#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:49
msgid "Terminal foundations"
msgstr "终端基础"

#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:51
msgid ""
"The compatibility model is a terminal receiving text and control sequences over a byte stream. "
"The following references explain the inherited vocabulary; they are not a claim that Silkie "
"implements every historical terminal feature."
msgstr "兼容模型是终端通过字节流接收文本和控制序列。以下参考资料解释了继承的术语；这不表示 Silkie 实现了所有历史终端功能。"

#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:55
msgid ""
"`ECMA-48: control functions <https://ecma-international.org/publications-and-"
"standards/standards/ecma-48/>`_ defines control-function syntax, including CSI, SGR, OSC, and "
"string terminators."
msgstr ""
"`ECMA-48：控制功能 <https://ecma-international.org/publications-and-standards/standards/ecma-48/>`_ "
"定义控制功能语法，包括 CSI、SGR、OSC 和字符串终止符。"

#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:58
msgid ""
"`XTerm control sequences <https://invisible-island.net/xterm/ctlseqs/ctlseqs.html>`_ covers the "
"VT/xterm conventions used for cursor movement, screen modes, mouse reporting, and other common "
"terminal interactions."
msgstr ""
"`XTerm 控制序列 <https://invisible-island.net/xterm/ctlseqs/ctlseqs.html>`_ "
"介绍光标移动、屏幕模式、鼠标报告及其他常见终端交互所用的 VT/xterm 约定。"

#: docs/silkie/developer-guide.rst:62
msgid ""
"`Silkie's terminfo source "
"<https://github.com/adamdeprince/silkie/blob/silkie/terminfo/kitty.terminfo>`_ describes the "
"capabilities advertised to terminfo-based applications."
msgstr ""
"`Silkie 的 terminfo 源码 "
"<https://github.com/adamdeprince/silkie/blob/silkie/terminfo/kitty.terminfo>`_ 描述向使用 terminfo "
"的应用公布的能力。"

